11.	To make his name famous for all time until distant days, 
12.	and to transmit to posterity and the days  
13.	to come the praise poems of his power, 
14.	the songs of his might, 
15.	and the lasting fame of his exceptional intelligence, 
16.	King @wRN{Šulgi}, 
17.	king of @wSN{Urim}, 
18.	has brought the songs' latent wisdom before the mighty son of @wDN{Ninsumun}. 
19.	He praises his own power in song, 
110.	and lauds his own superior native intelligence: 

{11 = 11-20}
1111.	I am a king, offspring begotten by a king and borne by a queen. 
1112.	I, @wRN{Šulgi} the noble, 
1113.	have been blessed with a favourable destiny right from the womb. 
1114.	When I was small, I was at the academy, 
1115.	where I learned the scribal art from the tablets of @wGN{Sumer} and @wGN{Akkad}. 
1116.	None of the nobles could write on clay as I could. 
1117.	There where people regularly went for tutelage in the scribal art, 
1118.	I qualified fully in subtraction, addition, reckoning and accounting. The fair @wDN{Nanibgal}, 
1119.	@wDN{Nisaba}, provided me amply with knowledge and comprehension. 
1120.	I am an experienced scribe who does not neglect a thing. 

{21 = 21-38}
2121.	When I sprang up, 
2122.	muscular as a cheetah, 
2123.	galloping like a thoroughbred ass at full gallop, 
2124.	the favour of @wDN{An} brought me joy; 
2125.	to my delight @wDN{Enlil} spoke favourably about me, 
2126.	and they gave me the sceptre because of my righteousness. 
2127.	I place my foot on the neck of the foreign lands; 
2128.	the fame of my weapons is established as far as the south, 
2129.	and my victory is established in the highlands. 
2130.	When I set off for battle and strife to a place that @wDN{Enlil} has commanded me, 
2131.	I go ahead of the main body of my troops and I clear the terrain for my scouts. 
2132.	I have a positive passion for weapons. 
2133.	Not only do I carry lance and spear, 
2134.	I also know how to handle slingstones with a sling. 
2135.	The clay bullets, 
2136.	the treacherous pellets that I shoot, 
2137.	fly around like a violent rainstorm. 
2138.	In my rage I do not let them miss. 

{39 = 39-51}
3939.	I sow fear and confusion in the foreign land. 
3940.	I look to my brother and friend, youthful @wDN{Utu}, 
3941.	as a source of divine encouragement. I, @wRN{Šulgi}, converse with him whenever he rises over there; 
3942.	he is the god who keeps a good eye on my battles. 
3943.	The youth @wDN{Utu}, beloved in the mountains, 
3944.	is the protective deity of my weapons; 
3945.	by his words I am strengthened and made pugnacious (?). 
3946.	In those battles, 
3947.	where weapon clashes on weapon, @wDN{Utu} shines on me. 
3948.	Thus I broke the weapons of the highlands over my knees, 
3949.	and in the south placed a yoke on the neck of @wGN{Elam}. 
3950.	I make the populations of the rebel lands -- how could they still resist my weapons? 
3951.	-- scatter like seed-grain over @wGN{Sumer} and @wGN{Akkad}. 

{52 = 52-55}
5252.	Let me boast of what I have done. 
5253.	The fame of my power is spread far and wide. 
5254.	My wisdom is full of subtlety. 
5255.	Do not my achievements surpass all qualifications? 

{56 = 56-76}
5656.	I stride forward in majesty, trampling endlessly through the esparto grass and thickets, 
5657.	capturing elephant after elephant, creatures of the plain; 
5658.	and I put an end to the heroic roaring in the plains of the different liona, 
5659.	the dragons of the plains, 
5660.	wherever it approaches from and wherever it is going. 
5661.	I do not go after them with a net, 
5662.	nor do I lie in wait for them in a hide; 
5663.	it comes to a confrontation of strength and weapons. 
5664.	I do not hurl a weapon; 
5665.	when I plunge a bitter-pointed lance in their throats, 
5666.	I do not flinch at their roar. 
5667.	I am not one to retreat to my hiding-place but, 
5668.	as when one warrior kills another warrior, I do everything swiftly on the open plain. 
5669.	In the desert where the paths peter out, 
5670.	I reduce the roar at the lair to silence. 
5671.	In the sheepfold and the cattle-pen, where heads are laid to rest (?), 
5672.	I put the shepherd tribesmen at ease. 
5673.	Let no one ever at any time say about me, 
5674.	@q{“Could he really subdue them all on his own?”} 
5675.	The number of lions that I have despatched with my weapons is limitless; 
5676.	their total is unknown. 

