154154.	I, @wRN{Šulgi}, king of @wSN{Urim}, have also devoted myself to the art of music. 
154155.	Nothing is too complicated for me; 
154156.	I know the full extent of the @fsux{tigi} and the @fsux{adab}, 
154157.	the perfection of the art of music. When I fix the frets on the lute, 
154158.	which enraptures my heart, I never damage its neck; 
154159.	I have devised rules for raising and lowering its intervals. 
154160.	On the @fsux{gu-uš} lyre I know the melodious tuning. 
154161.	I am familiar with the @fsux{sa-eš} and with drumming on its musical soundbox. 
154162.	I can take in my hands the @fsux{miritum}, which ……. 
154163.	I know the finger technique of the @fsux{alŋar} and @fsux{sabitum}, royal creations. 
154164.	In the same way I can produce sounds from the @fsux{urzababitum}, 
154165.	the @fsux{ḫarḫar}, the @fsux{zanaru}, the @fsux{ur-gula} and the @fsux{dim-lu-magura}. Even if they bring to me, 
154166.	as one might to a skilled musician, 
154167.	a musical instrument that I have not heard before, 
154168.	when I strike it up I make its true sound known; 
154169.	I am able to handle it just like something that has been in my hands before. 
154170.	Tuning, 
154171.	stringing, 
154172.	unstringing and fastening are not beyond my skills. 
154173.	I do not make the reed pipe sound like a rustic pipe, 
154174.	and on my own initiative I can wail a @fsux{šumunša} or make a lament as well as anyone who does it regularly. 

{175 = 175-189}
175175.	I bestow joy and gladness, 
175176.	and I pass my days in pomp and splendour. 
175177.	But people should consider for themselves -- it is a matter  
175178.	to keep in one's sights -- that at the inescapable end of life, 
175179.	no one will be spared the bitter gall of the land of oppression. 
175180.	But I am one who is powerful  
175181.	enough to trust in his own power. 
175182.	He who trusts in his own exalted name may carry out great things. 
175183.	Why should he do less? 
